title: 'pitfall : "soft procrastination" : focusing on what is nearly- but not most-important'
pid: d08c050c-ed49-4d61-afbd-d2994a702b0b
body: |2-
  Obvious procrastination substitutes obviously unproductive uses of time
  for better ones.
  On the other hand, if the substitutes are fairly productive,
  yet not the most productive, one might not recognize it as an error at all.
